{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm checking the committed AGENTS.md, which says there are no ADRs, so there's nothing to reconcile there. For the design badge I'll use text rendering, building the content from the icon and text and wrapping it in a pill with \"( \" and \" )\" borders.\n\nI'm settling on the badge's pill delimiters: the spec's `( ` and ` )` reads as parentheses with padding, so I'll build the badge as \"( text )\" and render it as a styled Text object that doesn't wrap.\n\nI'm working on the badge's measurement now, and I'm leaning toward using Text's own measurement or computing the cell length of the full rendered string with its borders, then clamping it to the available width.\n\nI'm working out how the badge measures itself: I'll lean on Measurement.get against the Text object, which handles the width clamp, and I'm considering a direct __rich_measure__ as the alternative. I'm also thinking about the streaming side, whether to yield from the Text's console render or delegate to console.render.\n\nI'm weighing whether to export Badge from the top-level rich package, since the top-level init doesn't import most classes eagerly, and I'm checking whether adding it to __all__ fits that pattern.\n\nI'm weighing a lazy import for Badge at the top level, using a module-level __getattr__ so importing rich doesn't pull in rich.text and the console machinery, and I'm checking whether a TYPE_CHECKING block is needed so mypy can still see the name.\n\nI'm checking whether the codebase already defines a module-level `__getattr__`, and I'm verifying that `Text.assemble` accepts `no_wrap`, `overflow`, and `end` keyword arguments. I'm also settling the styling split: the content and its inner spaces take the badge style, while the bracket characters take the border style.\n\nI'm going to confirm that Text.assemble accepts the no_wrap, overflow, and end keywords, and I'll check whether rich/__init__.py already defines a module-level __getattr__ before I write the file.\n\n","thinkingSignature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1oYWlrdS01LjUtMjAyNjEwMDd8Y2xhdWRlLW9uLWF3cyJ9"},{"type":"text","text":"The committed `AGENTS.md` says \"No ADRs found in this project\", so the project guidelines are the only architecture reference. I'll check the `Text.assemble` signature and confirm `rich/__init__.py` has no existing `__getattr__`, since I plan to use lazy export to avoid importing the console stack on `import rich`."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01Mtjs17MFzs6eGs7znu4ntt","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /app && grep -n \"def assemble\" -A 12 rich/text.py | head -20; grep -n \"__getattr__\" rich/__init__.py; grep -n \"def __rich_measure__\" -A4 rich/text.py | head"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"openrouter","model":"anthropic/claude-haiku-5.5","usage":{"input":2,"output":2210,"cacheRead":12347,"cacheWrite":2475,"totalTokens":17034,"cost":{"input":2.0000000000000002e-7,"output":0.0011049999999999999,"cacheRead":0.00012347,"cacheWrite":0.000309375,"total":0.001538045,"totalFromProvider":true},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":1979},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1794167931231,"providerThinkingLevel":"medium","responseId":"msg_011Cgr43JX8VtpQVzkUnL8Co","rawStopReason":"tool_use","durationMs":10854,"thinkingLevel":"medium"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01Mtjs17MFzs6eGs7znu4ntt","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"357:    def assemble(\n358-        cls,\n359-        *parts: Union[str, \"Text\", Tuple[str, StyleType]],\n360-        style: Union[str, Style] = \"\",\n361-        justify: Optional[\"JustifyMethod\"] = None,\n362-        overflow: Optional[\"OverflowMethod\"] = None,\n363-        no_wrap: Optional[bool] = None,\n364-        end: str = \"\\n\",\n365-        tab_size: int = 8,\n366-        meta: Optional[Dict[str, Any]] = None,\n367-    ) -> \"Text\":\n368-        \"\"\"Construct a text ins