{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The earlier error came from my own test: `from rich import *` overrode `print`, and I was printing the `Badge` class instead of an instance, so it's not renderable. Everything else checks out.\n\nI'm now sizing the \"日本\" cell: it's 4 cells wide, and with borders and padding the box should come to about 8 cells at most, with 4 as the minimum.\n\nI'm working out how a plain-text minimum width should behave here. Reporting the longest word undersells a badge that can't wrap, so I'm leaning toward setting both the minimum and maximum to the full cell width, clamped to the available space.\n\nI'm switching the measurement to report the badge's full cell width as both minimum and maximum, since a no-wrap badge can't shrink to its longest word, and clamping it to the available max width. I also need to import `cell_len` from `.cells` for that.\n\n","thinkingSignature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1oYWlrdS01LjUtMjAyNjEwMDd8Y2xhdWRlLW9uLWF3cyJ9"},{"type":"text","text":"Rendering works: standalone, in Table/Panel/Columns/Tree, and the top-level export. The final traceback is a bug in my test script (it printed the class, not an instance), not the component.\n\nOne real issue: the measurement reports `minimum=4` for `( 日本 )`, because `Text` uses the longest word as the minimum. The badge is `no_wrap`, so its minimum should be its full cell width, or a Table could shrink it below what it can display. I'll measure the full cell width directly."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01Ece1SUNrtqLqRUrF7vPf8j","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"/app/rich/badge.py","edits":[{"oldText":"from .measure import Measurement\n","newText":"from .cells import cell_len\nfrom .measure import Measurement\n"},{"oldText":"        return Measurement.get(console, options, self._text)","newText":"        # The badge never wraps, so its minimum width is its full cell width.\n        width = cell_l